Which quantitative measures are used to estimate disagreement in committee-based query strategies for deep active learning? Quantitative measures used to estimate disagreement in committee-based query strategies include:
- Vote entropy over the committee’s label votes;
- Kullback–Leibler (KL) divergence between the predictive label distributions of different committee members (or augmented views);
- Variation ratio (based on the fraction of committee members voting for the majority class);
- Var
